  "content": "# Bounded LRU Cache in Python: A Complete Tutorial\n\nAn **LRU (Least Recently Used)** cache evicts the least recently used item when the cache reaches its capacity. In Python, `collections.OrderedDict` provides an ideal foundation because it maintains insertion order and supports moving keys to the end in O(1) time, which is exactly what LRU semantics require.\n\nBelow is a complete, production-ready implementation with thorough explanation, edge cases, tests, a worked example, and complexity analysis.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The Core Idea\n\nIn an LRU cache:\n- **Most recent** items are at the **end** of the order.\n- **Least recent** items are at the **beginning** of the order.\n- On a `get`, we promote the accessed key to the most-recent position.\n- On a `put`, if the cache is full and the key doesn't already exist, we evict the first (least recently used) entry.\n\n`OrderedDict` gives us:\n- `move_to_end(key)` \u2014 promotes a key to the end (most recent).\n- `popitem(last=False)` \u2014 removes and returns the first (least recently used) item.\n\nBoth operations are O(1) in the average case (and worst case in CPython's C implementation).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Complete Implementation\n\n```python\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\nfrom typing import Any, Optional, Callable\n\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    \"\"\"\n    A bounded LRU cache backed by OrderedDict.\n\n    The most recently accessed/inserted item is kept; the least recently\n    used item is evicted when capacity is exceeded.\n\n    Complexity:\n        - get(key):   O(1) average / O(1) worst-case in CPython\n        - put(key,val):O(1) average / O(1) worst-case in CPython\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, capacity: int):\n        if capacity <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Capacity must be a positive integer.\")\n        self._capacity = capacity\n        self._store: OrderedDict[Any, Any] = OrderedDict()\n\n    def get(self, key: Any) -> Optional[Any]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Retrieve the value associated with `key`.\n\n        - If `key` is present, promote it to the most-recently-used position\n          and return its value.\n       ",
